    {
      "kind": "grammar_point",
      "external_id": "g_c1_tone_subtext_register_shift",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-tone-subtext-01",
        "slug": "c1-tone-subtext-register-shift",
        "title": "Shifting register deliberately",
        "rule_summary": "Adjust vocabulary, directness, contractions, and sentence structure to move appropriately between informal, neutral, and formal contexts.",
        "explanation": {
          "fa": "برای جابه‌جایی آگاهانه بین لحن خودمانی، خنثی و رسمی، واژگان، صراحت، contraction و ساختار جمله را تغییر می‌دهیم."
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "en": "Can we move this? → Would it be possible to reschedule the meeting?",
            "fa": "می‌شه جابه‌جاش کنیم؟ → آیا امکان تغییر زمان جلسه وجود دارد؟"
          },
          {
            "en": "That's not right. → That interpretation may not fully reflect the evidence.",
            "fa": "این درست نیست. → آن تفسیر ممکن است شواهد را به‌طور کامل بازتاب ندهد."
          }
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "grammar_point",
      "external_id": "g_c1_tone_subtext_diplomatic_language",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-tone-subtext-02",
        "slug": "c1-tone-subtext-diplomatic-language",
        "title": "Diplomatic challenge and disagreement",
        "rule_summary": "Challenge an idea rather than a person, acknowledge intent, and soften direct negatives while keeping the substantive point clear.",
        "explanation": {
          "fa": "به‌جای شخص، ایده را به چالش می‌کشیم؛ نیت را می‌پذیریم و بدون مبهم کردن اصل پیام، منفی مستقیم را نرم‌تر می‌کنیم."
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "en": "I see the logic, though I'm not convinced the assumption holds in this case.",
            "fa": "منطقش را می‌بینم، هرچند قانع نشده‌ام این فرض در این مورد برقرار باشد."
          },
          {
            "en": "That may be true in principle, but the practical constraints are different.",
            "fa": "در اصل شاید درست باشد، اما محدودیت‌های عملی متفاوت‌اند."
          }
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "grammar_point",
      "external_id": "g_c1_tone_subtext_cleft_sentences",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-tone-subtext-03",
        "slug": "c1-tone-subtext-cleft-sentences",
        "title": "Cleft sentences for focus",
        "rule_summary": "Use what-clauses and it-clefts to place deliberate emphasis on the most important part of a message.",
        "explanation": {
          "fa": "با what-clause و it-cleft بخش مهم پیام را برجسته می‌کنیم."
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "en": "What concerns me most is the lack of independent oversight.",
            "fa": "چیزی که بیشتر نگرانم می‌کند نبود نظارت مستقل است."
          },
          {
            "en": "It was the timing, rather than the decision itself, that caused the problem.",
            "fa": "زمان‌بندی بود، نه خود تصمیم، که مشکل را ایجاد کرد."
          }
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "external_id": "d_c1_tone_subtext_scene_1",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-tone-subtext-01",
        "title": "Tone, Subtext & Intent: part 1",
        "setting": "quiet cafe",
        "cefr": "C1",
        "topic": "polite-language",
        "characters": [
          "Noor",
          "Liam"
        ],
        "turns": [
          {
            "order": 1,
            "speaker": "Noor",
            "text": "What is the practical implication of that point?",
            "translation_fa": "پیامد عملی اون نکته چیه؟"
          },
          {
            "order": 2,
            "speaker": "Liam",
            "text": "I doubt the intent was dismissive, but the wording can easily come across that way.",
            "translation_fa": "فکر نمی‌کنم نیت بی‌اعتنایی بوده، ولی نحوه بیان خیلی راحت می‌تونه این‌طور برداشت بشه."
          },
          {
            "order": 3,
            "speaker": "Noor",
            "text": "Does the evidence justify going that far?",
